-------------------------------------------
0. PURPOSE & SCOPE
-------------------------------------------

ST-6.2 defines the format for all NPC schedule files.

Each NPC schedule:

- lives under `/ST-6/schedules/<handle>.md`
- describes when, where, and how an NPC moves during the four-day Merrivale run
- exposes tags the Narrative Engine uses to:
    - decide who is present
    - choose who can redirect the PC
    - determine emotional tone
    - open or close heat windows

Global timing lives in ST-6.1_Merrivale.md;  
NPC schedules must conform to that structure.

-------------------------------------------
1. FILE LOCATION & NAMING RULES
-------------------------------------------

All NPC schedules:

- must live in `/ST-6/schedules/`
- must be named `<handle>.md` to match ST-4 character folders

If a schedule file is missing, ST-7 falls back to:

- ST-6.1 global defaults  
- role-based availability templates  

